Package: calendar
Architecture: any
Depends:
 cinnamon (>= 6.4),
 infiltrator-calendar-resources (= ${binary:Version}),
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends}
Description: Cinnamon clock and calendar application
 Calendar integrates with Cinnamon's panel, popup, settings and calendar
 service while consuming the system-wide temporal capabilities exposed through
 Infiltrator Common. The application does not own installed calendar resource
 modules; removing Calendar therefore does not remove those system capabilities.
 .
 A platform-neutral C core handles conversion, grid construction, event
 intervals and precise scheduling. Thin native and JavaScript adapters provide
 Cinnamon integration. The same amd64 package can use the system ICU supplied
 by Ubuntu/Mint or Debian.

Package: infiltrator-calendar-resources
Architecture: any
Section: libs
Depends:
 libicu72 | libicu73 | libicu74 | libicu75 | libicu76 | libicu77 | libicu78 | libicu79 | libicu80 | libicu81,
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends}
Description: System-wide executable calendar and clock resources for InfiltratorOS
 Installs independently loadable calendar and clock capability modules under
 /System/Resources/Calendars and /System/Resources/Clocks. Libraries/Common
 owns discovery, validation, loading and both executable provider ABIs;
 Calendar, Files, System Settings, shell components and other consumers can
 use the same installed implementations.
 .
 This package is intentionally independent of the Calendar application and of
 System Settings so either application can be removed without removing the
 system calendar capabilities or the user's persisted temporal policy.
